WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.760
<b>Pirate Commodore Don Krieg</b>

38
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.760
So you're a pirate?

39
00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.760
Uh-huh.

40
00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.810
Is that why you went and
did a crazy thing like

41
00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.100
shoot a cannonball into the restaurant?

42
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.600
That was an accident!

43
00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.940
A stray shot?

44
00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.820
In any case, you really don't want
to do anything stupid to this place.

45
00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.070
The owner used to be a cook
in a famous pirate fleet.

46
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:17.160
Ohh... So the old man...
used to be a pirate...

47
00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.660
This restaurant is everything
to that crazy old man.

48
00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.540
It's the only treasure he'll
need for the rest of his life...

49
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:23.870
He'll do anything to protect it.

50
00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.590
On top of which, all of the cooks
who joined him out of respect and admiration

51
00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.460
are just as hot-headed as any pirate...

52
00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.630
Which helps since pirates are always
coming and going out of this place.

53
00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.430
Yeah, I've noticed that.

54
00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.010
This is a really wild
restaurant, huh?

55
00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.810
So true... And this is
how it is every day.

56
00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:45.190
It's gotten so bad that customers
are coming here just watch fights

57
00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.230
between the cooks and the pirates.

58
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.270
Every day, it's been a new
pirate ship and a new rampage.

59
00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.820
It wasn't long till all the
waiters got scared and bailed.

60
00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.110
Ah, that makes sense!

61
00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.990
So that's why the old man wanted
me to work for him for a year.

62
00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.030
So, you joining my pirate crew or what?

63
00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.790
I'm sorry, but I can't...

64
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.080
There's a reason I have to
work here in the restaurant,

65
00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.960
and so I can't just walk away from it.

66
00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:06.960
No way!

67
00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:07.830
I don't accept!

68
00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.710
What? You don't accept?!

69
00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:10.710
It's very simple.

70
00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.590
I refuse to accept your refusal!

71
00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:13.760
You're a good cook, and I need one,

72
00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.260
so it's obvious that we
should be pirates together.

73
00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.930
Listen to what I'm saying.

74
00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.300
I can't leave here, all right?

75
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.060
What's your reason for staying?

76
00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.970
I don't have to tell you anything!

77
00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:23.890
What the...?

78
00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.890
But you just said to listen to you!

79
00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.940
I told you my answer was no,
and that's all you need to hear from me.

80
00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.270
Now take your pirate ship, and
find a cook someplace else

81
00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.940
before I cut you up, Straw Hat!

82
00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.490
You listen to me, jerk.

83
00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:38.110
No one makes fun of my straw hat
unless they're ready for a beating!

84
00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.200
I'm sorry to interrupt...

85
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.330
What is it?!

86
00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:47.080
<b>Pirate Combatant Gin
Krieg Pirates</b>

87
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:45.120
My name is Ghin, and I'm a crew
member of Don Krieg's Pirate fleet...

88
00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.620
And you say that you're
a pirate yourself...

89
00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.000
What is it you seek?

90
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.210
Oh, the One Piece!

91
00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.420
And pretty soon, I'm gonna sail
the Grand Line and find it!

92
00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.420
Huh?

93
00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.590
Well, you can't have been
seeking it for long.

94
00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:03.100
If you don't even have a cook yet,
your crew can't be all that big.

95
00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.720
Nope, he's only the fifth member.

96
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.850
I told you I'm not going,
so don't count me!

97
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.860
You seem like a nice kid, so let me
give you some friendly advice, okay?

98
00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.440
The Grand Line is a
place you want to avoid.

99
00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.110
You're still young, there's
no need to rush into anything.

100
00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:19.780
Remember, the Grand Line is one
small part of this entire ocean.

101
00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.910
If you want to be a real
pirate, there are plenty of

102
00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:25.120
other places out here
on the seas to explore.

103
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.950
Hmm... I see...

104
00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.960
Well, why don't you just tell me
what to avoid in the Grand Line now?

105
00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.210
I can't...

106
00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.710
I don't know anything.

107
00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.500
I don't understand it.

108
00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.590
And that is why I fear it.

109
00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:41.680
For being a crewmember of
Don Krieg's, you're a pretty wimpy pirate.

110
00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.890
Hm? Who's Don Krieg?

111
00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:56.900
<b>Galley
Sea Restaurant</b>

112
00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.440
The appetizer
for table three is ready!

113
00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.650
Yeah, well you're gonna
have to take it out yourself,

114
00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.450
the last waiter's gone!

115
00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.360
You think more of them
will be comin', Patty?

116
00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.450
Who knows?

117
00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:06.950
I heard the guy you beat up earlier in
the restaurant was one of Don Krieg's men.

118
00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.870
I don't think that will make
the rest of them very happy.

119
00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.330
Heh... I don't care whose man he was.

120
00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.040
All I'm saying is, the stories
I've heard say Don Krieg is

121
00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.460
the strongest, fiercest and most evil
pirate in this part of the ocean.

122
00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.340
He is.

123
00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.340
Eh?

124
00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.680
On these waters, his grip
of fear reaches far and wide.

125
00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:33.400
He commands over fifty pirate captains,
one of the largest pirate fleets ever seen.

126
00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.940
He is truly... a monster.

127
00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.860
He doesn't scare me.

128
00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.820
I've heard that his extraordinary fleet

129
00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.660
of ships has more than
five thousand pirates.

130
00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.950
This could be bad for Boss Zeff...

131
00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.040
If that guy you beat up
goes to Don Krieg and

132
00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.710
tells him what you did,
and he sends just one ship...

133
00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.040
There won't be enough
of us to fight them off.

134
00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.710
We'll be crushed, like
a grape under an elephant,

135
00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.840
and left to sink to the
bottom of the ocean.

136
00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.050
Eh...

137
00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.890
You're saying I should have just served
him, so he could experience our

138
00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:08.430
great customer service
and meals for free?

139
00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:12.140
You don't think that would have been rude
to the other damn crooks who pay money?

140
00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.480
I would never stoop that low!

141
00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:17.400
This is the Baratie.

142
00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.940
The fighting cooks have a
reputation to uphold, don't we?

143
00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:24.530
I'd never ruin that. I don't
care who that pirate cries to.

144
00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.030
Let them send their ships.
I'll fight them all off.

145
00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.540
If you're scared, quit and
let the real cooks work.

146
00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:30.790
Don't you dare say that to me!

147
00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.910
I'm tired of all that
big talk you spit out,

148
00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.040
which is why all the
waiters jumped ship!

149
00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.920
Everything that's happening
now is all your fault, Patty!

150
00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:38.840
Please!

151
00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:43.720
Those waiters were worthless wimps the moment
a customer showed up! Worthless wimps!

152
00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.510
Go for it!

153
00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:46.840
Take him out, Carne!

154
00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.220
He doesn't stand a chance, Patty!

155
00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.680
All right, what's all this?

156
00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.980
Get back to work already!

157
00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.520
Yes, Boss Zeff!

158
00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.860
So long, then.

159
00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.020
Thanks for the warning,

160
00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.860
but I'm still gonna
go to the Grand Line.

161
00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:01.650
I know.

162
00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.240
Do whatever you want.

163
00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.700
I'm just a stranger, and I can't stop you
from going anywhere you wanna go.

164
00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.330
I just wanted to give
you a fair warning.

165
00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.540
And to you, Chef...
Thank you for everything.

166
00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.710
You saved my life,
and I owe you for that.

167
00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.540
Your cooking skills are
the best I've ever seen.

168
00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.880
I hope to come back again sometime.

169
00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.420
I'll have a seat for you.

170
00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.470
Chore Boy, get up here right now!

171
00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:27.510
Boss Zeff!

172
00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.140
You're hard to find.

173
00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.230
Hey, Ghin... Go.

174
00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.440
Sorry...

175
00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.440
You'll probably get yelled at or fired
'cause you gave me that food for free...

176
00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.610
Whatever...

177
00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.160
Hmm...

178
00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.290
Now there's not proof, so there's
no way for me to get yelled at.

179
00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:02.630
Try not to get
caught again, you hear?

180
00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:04.670
Thank you again, Chef Sanji!

181
00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.670
I will never forget your kindness!

182
00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:10.930
Sanji! Chore Boy!

183
00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.180
Get back to work already!

184
00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:15.890
Hey, table three is ready!

185
00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:23.230
<b>Monkey D. Luffy
Unpaid Cabin Boy
Sea Restaurant</b>

186
00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.020
Hey, guys!

187
00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:23.230
My name's Luffy, and I'm gonna
be the new chore boy around here.

188
00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:24.940
Nice to meet all of you!

189
00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.240
<b>On Hiatus From Piracy</b>

190
00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.700
<b>On Hiatus From Piracy</b>

191
00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.910
<b>On Hiatus From Piracy</b>

192
00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.870
<b>On Hiatus From Piracy</b>

193
00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:40.880
What happened to that dessert?

194
00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.920
<b>On Hiatus From Piracy</b>

195
00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.300
Which one of us was
supposed to make that?

196
00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:46.800
It was supposed to be him!

197
00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.180
I don't have time to
make that, I'm too busy!

198
00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.760
You're too busy being a jerk!

199
00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.970
Say that again, I dare you!

200
00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.680
<b>On Hiatus From Piracy</b>

201
00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.720
Don't just sit
there picking your nose!

202
00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.640
Go wash the dishes or
something... Right now!

203
00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.940
Has anyone seen Sanji?

204
00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.900
I think I saw
him hittin' on a customer.

205
00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:04.900
Again?!

206
00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.860
I wish Boss Zeff would get rid of him!

207
00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:10.740
It's bad enough he's the Sous Chef,
but he's never in the kitchen doing his job!

208
00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.410
I think we're stuck with him.

209
00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.240
He's worked here longer than any of us.

210
00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.750
He was working the kitchen and
the dining room even before I started.

211
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.960
Yeah, but even so,
I just don't get it.

212
00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:21.330
Why does he stay here when

213
00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.460
he and Boss Zeff are always fighting?

214
00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.750
I think he wants
to be the Head Chef.

215
00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.930
Hmm?

216
00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:28.630
Huh?

217
00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:31.880
Chore Boy!

218
00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.640
Just how many of these dishes have
you gone and broken into tiny pieces?!

219
00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:36.720
You know what?

220
00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.720
I forgot to count! Aw, man...

221
00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.810
I wasn't being serious, you idiot!

222
00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:41.980
Why are you breaking them?!

223
00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:45.110
Stop screwing around,
and clean up your mess.

224
00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:47.020
That, I can do!

225
00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:47.730
Ahh...

226
00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.440
Stop! Don't take the food!

227
00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.400
What's wrong with you?!

228
00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:53.740
That was a perfect entree!

229
00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.780
Yep! Pretty tasty!

230
00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.500
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

231
00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.460
Get out of our kitchen!

232
00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.460
Why don't we have you take
orders in the dining room?

233
00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.670
Just ask the customers
what they want to eat.

234
00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.300
Is that simple enough?

235
00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.590
Yes.

236
00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.880
These chores sure are boring.

237
00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.600
Wonder if Koby got tired
of all this work, too.

238
00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:17.470
Chore Boy!

239
00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.390
What are you doing?!

240
00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.810
We heard you had to work
here for a whole year.

241
00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.230
Is it okay if we redraw
the flag for our ship?

242
00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:27.270
You're eating all
this delicious food without me?

243
00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.650
What kind of crew are you?

244
00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:30.730
How could you do this to me?!

245
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.860
Hold on... I think that's our
business, isn't that right?

246
00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:34.780
Take this.

247
00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.120
Oh, boy... This is gonna be so good.

248
00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.540
You know, I have to say the food
here is really quite delicious.

249
00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.750
Good stuff...

250
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:44.670
Yes, it is...

251
00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.670
I feel bad for you, but...

252
00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.800
You should be drinking this yourself!

253
00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:55.050
I can't believe you did that!

254
00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:58.550
Yeah, well, I can't
believe you did that!

255
00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.260
Aw, that was nasty!

256
00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.690
Aren't they... quaint...

257
00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:10.570
I wonder if that's
the rest of his crew.

258
00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.740
Finish pouring it yourself.

259
00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:23.160
Oh, dear ocean, thank you for this
treasure you have shared from your depths.

260
00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.040
Huh?

261
00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:25.920
Ah, yes, my love...

262
00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.500
I can't bear this hardship
of loving you from afar.

263
00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.750
It is too difficult.

264
00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:33.130
I am now prepared to sail to the
ends of the earth as a pirate

265
00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:36.720
if it means someone of your
rare beauty will be by my side!

266
00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:41.060
To be together sailing the seas!

267
00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:44.270
But how tragic a great
obstacle blocks our way.

268
00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:47.690
And that great
obstacle would be me, right?

269
00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:48.810
Sanji...

270
00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.560
Stupid geezer.

271
00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.980
This is an opportunity you
don't want to pass up.

272
00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.780
Why not join them and become a pirate?

273
00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.740
I have no need to keep
you here at my restaurant.

274
00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:16.170
I see...

275
00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:21.550
This cook saved your life, and you
were able to return here to us.

276
00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:26.180
Is that what you are saying... Ghin?

277
00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:29.350
Y... Yes... but you see...

278
00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:33.230
I had no idea the main ship was
in this condition, Don Krieg...

279
00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.650
No idea.

280
00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.610
So, what now?

281
00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:42.660
Now, I believe I'll take you
to the Sea Restaurant Baratie.

282
00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:50.670
Hey, listen, pal...
I'm the Sous Chef in this place.

283
00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:53.630
What do you mean you
don't need me any more?

284
00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.670
You fight with customers
all the time...

285
00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.880
You flirt with every woman under
eighty who walks through here...

286
00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.340
You can't even cook a decent meal...

287
00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:04.140
You're worth less to me than
the chum after brunch...

288
00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.640
That's what I mean.

289
00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.470
So... uh...

290
00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:14.980
Oh, and let's not forget about how
the other cooks avoid you like you were poison.

291
00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:20.030
So just run off and be a pirate or whatever,
but get out of this restaurant!

292
00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.530
That's how it is?

293
00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.870
You shoot off at the mouth and expect
that I'm just going to take it, old man?

294
00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:34.380
I could blow off everything you said,
but I won't listen to anyone trash my cooking!

295
00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:37.840
I'm staying here as a
Sous Chef, and that's final!

296
00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.630
You hear me?!

297
00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.890
What do you think you're doing,
grabbing your boss by the collar?!

298
00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.680
You ingrate!

299
00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:54.610
You can try to kick me out...

300
00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:58.440
But I'm here to stay. I'm not
going anywhere, old man.

301
00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.150
Not till you're dead and gone!

302
00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.360
Dead? Hah.

303
00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.530
I got another hundred years
of kickin' your ass left in me!

304
00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.580
He's always
gotta have the last word.

305
00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.240
See? He said it's cool.

306
00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.370
Now you can become a pirate!

307
00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:10.950
Shut up!

308
00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.870
My apologies...

309
00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:17.460
I hope I can make it up to you with this
delightful fruit Macedonia, my princess.

310
00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.670
Wow! You're too kind!
It looks wonderful.

311
00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:21.420
Good.

312
00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.590
Hey! Don't forget about
us, Mister Casanova!

313
00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:26.220
We'd better get some
kind of an apology, too!

314
00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:28.930
This tea should be more
than adequate for you...

315
00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.770
In fact, you should be thanking me.

316
00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:32.230
What?! You wanna fight?

317
00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:34.060
You're gonna regret this!

318
00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.650
Take him out, Zoro!

319
00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.190
You take him out!

320
00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:39.690
Stop it! Please don't
fight because of me.

321
00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:40.690
Of course, my dear...

322
00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.530
Who said it was about you?!

323
00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.030
I wanted to tell you that...

324
00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:44.700
Yeah?

325
00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:47.030
That all of the food
here is just delicious...

326
00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.410
But it's a little too expensive for me.

327
00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.740
Relax, it's free.

328
00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.960
Oh! Thank you!

329
00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:54.420
You guys still gotta pay, though.

330
00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.120
What?!

331
00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.880
How very generous of you.

332
00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.300
What are you sitting around for?!

333
00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:04.430
You're not here to lounge around.

334
00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:05.550
Right...

335
00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:12.470
<b>Two Days Later</b>

336
00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.250
It's them... They're here!

337
00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.420
The hourglasses mean our time is up!

338
00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.300
What are we gonna do now?!

339
00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.050
That flag means death!

340
00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:52.640
There's no doubt; it belongs to the
ruler of the East Blue... Don Krieg!

341
00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:10.370
But why? Why have
the Krieg Pirates come here?!

342
00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:13.290
I told you! I knew those
goons would show up!

343
00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.290
Now are you gonna get rid
of those guys or what?!

344
00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:17.920
This can't be real! He's got
a whole fleet to command.

345
00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:21.420
Why would Don Krieg come here to
get revenge for just one man?

346
00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:23.340
I mean, doesn't he have
anything better to do?

347
00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:26.670
He's here, all right! We're not
imagining that ship, are we?!

348
00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:30.180
Guys, don't panic, but I think this
is our cue to leave, right now!

349
00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:32.640
Look at the sheer size of that galleon!

350
00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.860
What a huge ship!

351
00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.940
You think Ghin came back to
repay you for your kindness?

352
00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.280
I seriously doubt that's it.

353
00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.110
– It's something else.
– Hm?

354
00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:58.910
Hey, look!

355
00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.420
Yeah... Their ship...

356
00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.340
Whoa, what'd they do?

357
00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.390
Sail through a hurricane or something?

358
00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:14.890
Doesn't seem like damage
inflicted by cannons.

359
00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:17.890
In fact, it doesn't
look man-made at all.

360
00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:22.350
Hmm, then maybe
it was a tornado-hurricane!

361
00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.520
There he is...

362
00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:44.840
<b>Don Krieg
Pirate Commodore</b>

363
00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.960
I beg you...

364
00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:53.470
I need food... and water...

365
00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:55.430
We have money...

366
00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:57.220
Lots of money...

367
00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.850
No, this can't be!

368
00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.980
Where's the death and destruction?

369
00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:07.190
Is this really the Don Krieg,
Commodore of the grand pirate fleet?

370
00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:10.610
Guess he's hungry.

371
00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.410
C... Captain!

372
00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.960
Don Krieg!

373
00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:25.790
Please, help him! Our captain
is on the brink of starvation!

374
00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.960
He could die!

375
00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.340
He hasn't had a single
bite to eat for days!

376
00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:32.510
He'll die if he doesn't
get some food soon!

377
00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:41.270
This is great!

378
00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:43.850
I haven't laughed that
hard in a long time.

379
00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:46.610
The great Don Krieg,
kneeling before us!

380
00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:48.150
We have some money!

381
00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:49.860
We're here as customers this time!

382
00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.990
Do you really think I'm that stupid?

383
00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:54.360
Hey! Get a hold of
the marines right away.

384
00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.160
What?!

385
00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.200
He's finally weak
enough to be captured.

386
00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.580
This may never happen again,
and I'm not gonna ruin it

387
00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:01.290
by helping him get his strength back!

388
00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.710
He's right!

389
00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:05.710
Who knows what he'll do if
gets on his feet again?

390
00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.580
He's done terrible things!

391
00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.090
And as soon as he's
up, he'll keep on doin' 'em.

392
00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:12.340
I say we let him starve.

393
00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:16.470
Once he's back to normal, he'll kill
every last person in this restaurant.

394
00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:20.680
He won't get so much as
a glass of water from me.

395
00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.810
I won't do anything...

396
00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.850
I won't do anything...

397
00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.650
Once I eat...

398
00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:32.480
I promise I'll leave quietly...

399
00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:35.700
So please... Be merciful, and help me...

400
00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:38.160
You're a king, Don Krieg, stop it!

401
00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:40.530
Please, don't reduce yourself to this!

402
00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.870
You're better than the common beggar!

403
00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:45.040
Please, sir! What about your pride?

404
00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.370
I promise...

405
00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.750
Please... I'll take the scraps.

406
00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.090
I'll take anything...

407
00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:55.130
Anything...

408
00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:58.970
Don...

409
00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.060
Heh, boo-hoo for the cruel pirate.

410
00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.100
Hey, step aside, Patty.

411
00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.360
Whoa!

412
00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.150
Huh?

413
00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:18.990
Sanji...

414
00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:19.990
Huh?

415
00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:23.660
Here's something for your captain.

416
00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.580
Thank you, Sanji.

417
00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.510
Thank you!

418
00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:47.350
You dimwit!

419
00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.350
Get that food away from him right now!

420
00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.730
Don't you realize he's a cold,
heartless, killing machine?!

421
00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:55.530
This is the man known as
the ruler of the East Blue,

422
00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:57.570
the most treacherous of all pirates!

423
00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:01.660
It all started back in prison...

424
00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.410
He pretended to be a Marine...

425
00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:06.240
And when he decided to
declare his pirate ambitions,

426
00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:10.170
he took command of a Marine vessel
by killing the senior officer!

427
00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:14.290
He would raise the
Marine flag to enter ports,

428
00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:18.300
then lay waste to the unsuspecting
cities and passenger ships there.

429
00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:21.260
He even showed the white flag
before attacking enemy ships.

430
00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.510
He did anything to secure victory.

431
00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.970
That guy fights dirty.

432
00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.810
He's also unmatched
in physical combat.

433
00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:32.940
You think he'll just leave us alone?

434
00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:35.150
Well, I've got news for you!

435
00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:38.990
That's not possible with a
bloodthirsty killer like him!

436
00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:40.240
He deserves death!

437
00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:00.300
Sanji!

438
00:22:08.100 --> 00:22:10.390
This is not what we agreed on!

439
00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:13.140
You gave me your word! I only
brought you here because

440
00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:16.440
you promised that you
wouldn't ruin this place!

441
00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:18.280
Or hurt the man who saved us!

442
00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:24.910
Yes, that was delicious.

443
00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:28.370
I feel alive again.

444
00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:44.380
Hey... You see that?

445
00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:47.220
It looks bad...

446
00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:49.220
What do you think is going on in there?

447
00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:50.770
Don't know. Let's go inside and see.

448
00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:52.560
What?! Are you serious?!

449
00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:56.980
This is a pretty good ship...

450
00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:59.570
I believe that I'll take it.

451
00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:05.700
Right... I see...

452
00:23:14.460 --> 00:23:17.830
As you can all see, my ship is a wreck.

453
00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:20.380
Naturally, I'll be
needing a nice new one.

454
00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:22.050
After a few small chores...

455
00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:24.800
Every last one of you
will leave the ship.

456
00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:26.220
What?! No!

457
00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:30.100
Don Krieg... You promised... Please!

458
00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:38.560
There are about a hundred men left
onboard my ship, all are weak with hunger,

459
00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:40.650
and many are seriously wounded.

460
00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:46.240
If you value your lives, you will prepare
food and water for every last one of them.

461
00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:50.200
I've lost too many
men to hunger already...

462
00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:54.250
Water...

463
00:23:55.710 --> 00:23:58.040
Bring them over immediately!

464
00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:01.800
You're telling us to
feed our executioners?!

465
00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:06.050
Do you hear how stupid
that sounds?! We refuse!

466
00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:07.720
You refuse?

467
00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:09.640
I wasn't asking you.

468
00:24:09.640 --> 00:24:14.350
Now make no mistake, you wretched
cook, I'm not placing an order...

469
00:24:14.350 --> 00:24:15.850
I am giving you one!

470
00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:21.440
Do I make myself clear?!
Don't defy me...!

471
00:24:26.950 --> 00:24:28.610
Sanji...

472
00:24:29.490 --> 00:24:31.740
Sanji... Sorry...

473
00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:34.330
I didn't mean for this to happen.

474
00:24:34.330 --> 00:24:35.750
You see?!

475
00:24:35.750 --> 00:24:38.420
Look what you brought on this
restaurant, you stupid bastard!

476
00:24:51.590 --> 00:24:52.390
Hey!

477
00:24:57.520 --> 00:24:59.190
Where do you think you're going?!

478
00:25:01.150 --> 00:25:03.020
To the kitchen...

479
00:25:03.020 --> 00:25:05.940
Looks like I'll be cooking
a hundred more meals today.

480
00:25:06.900 --> 00:25:08.530
Sanji!

481
00:25:08.530 --> 00:25:11.910
What?! Are you crazy?!

482
00:25:11.910 --> 00:25:14.830
Good... Hop to it.

483
00:25:19.620 --> 00:25:22.290
Tell me the truth, Sanji!
Are you his spy or something?!

484
00:25:22.290 --> 00:25:24.840
We can't let you go
anywhere near that kitchen.

485
00:25:24.840 --> 00:25:26.670
We're fed up
with you acting insane!

486
00:25:29.590 --> 00:25:31.050
All right...

487
00:25:31.680 --> 00:25:33.390
Stop me if you wish.

488
00:25:37.310 --> 00:25:38.310
I know...

489
00:25:39.390 --> 00:25:43.860
It's no secret that Don Krieg
is a terrible, ruthless man.

490
00:25:43.860 --> 00:25:46.110
Huh?

491
00:25:46.110 --> 00:25:48.230
But that doesn't matter to me...

492
00:25:49.360 --> 00:25:50.900
It doesn't matter!

493
00:25:51.820 --> 00:25:56.330
After we feed all these men, who
knows what's going to happen...

494
00:25:56.330 --> 00:25:59.500
I am just a simple cook,
no more and no less.

495
00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:02.830
If someone's going hungry,
it's my duty to feed them.

496
00:26:02.830 --> 00:26:04.540
That's all I know...

497
00:26:05.920 --> 00:26:08.090
Whaddya say?

498
00:26:08.090 --> 00:26:09.420
Is that wrong?

499
00:26:17.140 --> 00:26:18.220
Patty!

500
00:26:18.220 --> 00:26:20.180
Hey! Somebody grab him!

501
00:26:21.230 --> 00:26:26.820
You bring free food to the bums I kick
outta this place, over and over again...

502
00:26:26.820 --> 00:26:30.650
And I'm not about to argue over who's
right in that particular situation,

503
00:26:30.650 --> 00:26:33.780
but this time, you're just
flat out wrong, Sanji.

504
00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:36.320
I can't let you do things
like that anymore.

505
00:26:36.320 --> 00:26:38.410
We're going to protect this place.

506
00:26:38.410 --> 00:26:40.660
Fortunately, we've got
numbers on our side.

507
00:26:41.330 --> 00:26:45.040
It is Don Krieg, but what
could he do against all of us?

508
00:26:46.170 --> 00:26:50.380
At a joint like this, pirate
scumbags come and go all day.

509
00:26:50.380 --> 00:26:53.680
We're fully prepared to
serve any kind of customer!

510
00:26:53.680 --> 00:26:54.840
Is that...?

511
00:26:54.840 --> 00:27:00.560
I really hope you saved some room for
dessert... 'cause I have a secret recipe...

512
00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:01.470
Huh?

513
00:27:01.470 --> 00:27:04.270
... that is truly to die for!

514
00:27:04.270 --> 00:27:09.020
Open wide! Here comes
the Meat Ball of Doom!

515
00:27:19.280 --> 00:27:21.080
Don!

516
00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:27.540
Don!

517
00:27:32.760 --> 00:27:34.800
I might've broken the door...

518
00:27:34.800 --> 00:27:37.010
I sure hope Zeff doesn't
yell at me again.

519
00:27:37.010 --> 00:27:40.890
He might go easy on you for
saving the restaurant and all.

520
00:27:41.470 --> 00:27:44.980
So what are we going to do about
all the guys left in Krieg's ship?

521
00:27:44.980 --> 00:27:49.310
Fry 'em! Cover it in batter,
and fry the entire thing.

522
00:27:49.310 --> 00:27:53.230
Are you a chef or a comedian?

523
00:27:53.230 --> 00:27:55.820
Because your jokes are lame!

524
00:27:56.530 --> 00:27:59.030
And that dessert was terrible!

525
00:28:00.030 --> 00:28:02.160
The worst I ever had!

526
00:28:07.290 --> 00:28:10.040
So die!

527
00:28:15.590 --> 00:28:17.430
He's got 'em everywhere!

528
00:28:17.430 --> 00:28:18.550
All those guns!

529
00:28:31.650 --> 00:28:34.650
You cooks should not have defied me!

530
00:28:35.650 --> 00:28:40.160
I am by far the world's strongest man!

531
00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:42.370
Arms, made of solid steel!

532
00:28:42.370 --> 00:28:45.500
Wootz steel body armor, impenetrable!

533
00:28:45.500 --> 00:28:50.000
And a diamond fist that could
pound this entire world to dust.

534
00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:52.210
In addition to the weapons on my body,

535
00:28:52.210 --> 00:28:56.050
I have a fleet of fifty ships
with five thousand pirates!

536
00:28:56.050 --> 00:28:57.470
My record is perfect!

537
00:28:57.470 --> 00:29:00.840
I've won every single battle
that I've ever been in!

538
00:29:00.840 --> 00:29:02.550
I am Don!

539
00:29:02.550 --> 00:29:06.140
And I'm the only one
fit to be called Don!

540
00:29:06.140 --> 00:29:07.850
Outta the way, kid.

541
00:29:07.850 --> 00:29:10.140
Wha... Uh!

542
00:29:10.140 --> 00:29:15.980
When I give you slime balls an order,
you will follow it down to the last letter!

543
00:29:15.980 --> 00:29:18.320
Don't you ever disobey me!

544
00:29:21.570 --> 00:29:23.950
This is about a hundred meals...

545
00:29:23.950 --> 00:29:26.080
Now take it to your men right away.

546
00:29:26.080 --> 00:29:27.540
No, Owner Zeff!

547
00:29:29.710 --> 00:29:33.080
You're... Red Foot Zeff.

548
00:29:37.010 --> 00:29:40.510
Wha... What're you doing?!
You can't be serious!

549
00:29:40.510 --> 00:29:42.590
If all of those
pirates get their strength back,

550
00:29:42.590 --> 00:29:45.600
the restaurant will be
completely taken over!

551
00:29:45.600 --> 00:29:49.480
That would be true... if they
still had the will to fight.

552
00:29:50.690 --> 00:29:52.560
Tell me...

553
00:29:52.560 --> 00:29:54.940
Did your will survive defeat?

554
00:29:57.900 --> 00:29:59.650
That... can't be...

555
00:29:59.650 --> 00:30:02.610
The great Don Krieg was defeated?

556
00:30:02.610 --> 00:30:05.620
Whoa... Not even he could do it.

557
00:30:05.620 --> 00:30:09.290
A pirate fleet with fifty ships
couldn't make it on the Grand Line!

558
00:30:09.870 --> 00:30:10.620
The Grand Line?

559
00:30:10.620 --> 00:30:13.120
It is you, isn't it?

560
00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:15.920
You're Red Foot Zeff!

